G2326.def:
θερισμός, -οῦ, ὁ
(θερίζω), [in LXX chiefly for קָצִיר ;] 
harvest; 
__(a) the act: Jean 4:35; 
__(b) the time: fig., Matthieu 13:30, 39, Marc 4:29 
__(with) the crop: figuratively, Matthieu 9:37-38, Luc 10:2, Apocalypse 14:15.†

G2344.def:
θησαυρός, -οῦ, ὁ
(τίθημι), [in LXX chiefly for אוֹצָר ;] 
__1. a place of safe keeping; 
__(a) a casket: Matthieu 2:11; 
__(b) a treasury (1Ma.3:29 and frequently in cl.); 
__(with) a storehouse (Néhémie 13:12, Deutéronome 28:12, al.): Matthieu 13:52; metaphorically, of the soul, Matthieu 12:35; τ. καρδίας, Luc 6:45 
__2. a treasure: Matthieu 6:18-21 13:44, Luc 12:33-34, Hébreux 11:26; θ. ἐν οὐρανῷ (see Dalman, Words, 206 ff.), Matthieu 19:21, Marc 10:21, Luc 18:22; of the knowledge of God through Christ, 2 Corinthiens 4:7; τ. σοφίας κ. γνώσεως, Colossiens 2:3.†

G2359.def:
θρίξ, τριχός, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for שֵׂעָר ;] 
hair; 
__(a) of the head: Matthieu 3:4 5:36 10:30, Luc 7:38, 44 12:7 21:18, Jean 11:2 12:3, Actes 27:34, 1 Pierre 3:3, Apocalypse 1:14; 
__(b) of animals: Marc 1:6, Apocalypse 9:8.†

G2364.def:
θυγάτηρ, -τρός, ἡ
(for use of vocat., cf. M, Pr., 71; WH, App, 158), [in LXX for בַּת (Genèse 5:4, al.), exc. Juges 21:14 B, 2 Chroniques 21:17 (אִשָּׁה ;] 
daughter: Matthieu 9:18 10:35, 37 14:6 15:22, 28, Marc 5:35 6:22 7:26, 29, Luc 2:36 8:42, 49 12:53, Actes 2:17" (LXX) Actes 7:21 21:9, Hébreux 11:24. In NT, as in OT, not in cl.; 
__(a) as a form of friendly address (cf. Ruth 2:2, 22 al.): Matthieu 9:22, Marc 5:34, Luc 8:48; 
__(b) metaphorically: sc. κυρίου, 2 Corinthiens 6:18 (cf. Ésaïe 43:6); 
__(with) of posterity: θ. Ἀαρών, Luc 1:5; Ἀβραάμ, Luc 13:16 (cf. Ésaïe 16:2, 4Ma.15:28, al); 
__(d) of habita­tion: θ. Σιών, Ἱερουσαλήμ, Matthieu 21:5 (LXX), Luc 23:28, Jean 12:15 (cf. Ésaïe 1:8, Zacharie 9:9, al.).†

G2379.def:
θυσιαστήριον, -ου, τό
(θυσιάζω, to sacrifice), [in LXX (where the word first appears) very freq., nearly always for מַדְבַּח ;] 
an altar: 
__(a) generally, Jacques 2:21; pl., Romains 11:3 (LXX); metaphorically, Hébreux 13:10 (see Westc., in l, and esp. his add, note on the history of the word, 455 ff.); 
__(b) of the altar of burnt-offering in the Temple, Matthieu 5:23-24 23:18-20, 35, Luc 11:51, 1 Corinthiens 9:13 10:18, Hébreux 7:13, Apocalypse 11:1; 
__(with) of the altar of incense in the sanctuary (Exode 30:1, al.), Luc 1:11; symbolically in Heaven, Apocalypse 6:9 8:3 9:13 14:18 16:7 (Cremer, 292).†

G2398.def:
ἴδιος, -α, -ον (in Attic usually -ος, -ον), 
[in LXX chiefly for of person(s) suff., also for לָהֶם, etc.; (τὰ ἴ.) בֵּיתוֹ ;] 
__1. one's own; 
__(a) of that which is private and personal (in cl. opposite to κοινός, δημόσιος; cf. infr. 3); 
__(b) of property, friends, home, country, etc. (in cl. opposite to ἀλλότριος; in late writers often, like ἑαυτοῦ, with weakened sense, see M, Pr., 87ff.; Deiss., BS, 123f.): Luc 6:41, Jean 1:42 5:43, Actes 2:6 20:28, 1 Corinthiens 11:21, Galates 6:5, 2 Timothée 1:9, Hébreux 7:27, Ju 6, al.; πράσσειν τὰ ἴ., 1 Thessaloniciens 4:11; κατὰ τὰς ἰ. ἐπιθυμίας, 2 Timothée 4:3; οἱ ἴδιοι, Jean 1:11 (M, Pr., 90f.; Field, Notes, 84) 13:1, Actes 4:23, 1 Timothée 5:8; τὰ ἴδια, one's home (Field, Notes, l.with), Luc 18:28, Jean 1:11 16:32 19:27. 
__2. peculiar, distinct, appropriate, proper: τὸ ἴ. σῶμα, 1 Corinthiens 15:38; ἐν τ. ἰ. τάγματι, 1 Corinthiens 15:23; εἰς τ. τόπον τ. ἴ., Actes 1:25; = αὐτοῦ (see Deiss., ut. supr.), Matthieu 22:5, Jean 1:42 (cf. Wis.10:1). 
__3. Adverbially (see supr., 1 (a); and cf. WM, 739:2); 
__(a) ἰδίᾳ, severally, separately: 1 Corinthiens 12:11; 
__(b) κατ᾽ ἰδίαν, apart, privately, in private: Matthieu 14:13, 23 20:17, Marc 4:34 7:33, Luc 10:23, Actes 23:19, al.
